//RS 
//RS /// One declared row shape, for schema derivation: a struct's generic parameter
//RS /// names in source order, then its `(field, declared type)` list in source
//RS /// order.
//RS ///
//RS /// The AST comptime interpreter reads `StructDef`s; the canonical TIR
//RS /// evaluator reads sema's registered field/type tables. Both hand the same
//RS /// facts to the one kernel below, so neither tier owns a schema of its own.
//RS pub type SchemaRow<'f> = &'f dyn Fn(&str) -> Option<(Vec<String>, Vec<(String, Type)>)>;
//RS 
